{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include<bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\ntypedef long long ll;\nconst int N = 266666;\nint n, k, MOD;\nll fact[N], inv_fact[N], dp[30][22], arr[18][N], b[N];\n\nll power(ll base, ll exp) {\n    ll result = 1;\n    base %= MOD;\n    while (exp) {\n        if (exp & 1) result = (result * base) % MOD;\n        base = (base * base) % MOD;\n        exp >>= 1;\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    scanf(\"%d %d %d\", &n, &k, &MOD);\n    if (n % 2 == 1) {\n        cout << power(k, n) << \"\\n\";\n        return 0;\n    }\n    fact[0] = 1;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) fact[i] = fact[i-1] * i % MOD;\n    inv_fact[n] = power(fact[n], MOD-2);\n    for (int i = n-1; i >= 0; --i) inv_fact[i] = inv_fact[i+1] * (i+1) % MOD;\n    n >>= 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i <= n; ++i) {\n        int pc = __builtin_popcount(i);\n        arr[pc][i] = inv_fact[i*2];\n    }\n    for (int i = 0; i < 17; ++i)\n        for (int bit = 0; bit < 17; ++bit)\n            for (int mask = 0; mask < (1 << 17); ++mask)\n                if ((mask >> bit) & 1)\n                    arr[i][mask] += arr[i][mask ^ (1 << bit)];\n    for (int i = 0; i < 17; ++i)\n        for (int mask = 0; mask < (1 << 17); ++mask)\n            arr[i][mask] %= MOD;\n    int target = __builtin_popcount(n);\n    for (int mask = 0; mask < (1 << 17); ++mask) {\n        memset(dp, 0, sizeof(dp));\n        dp[0][0] = 1;\n        for (int j = 1; j <= k; ++j) {\n            for (int u = 0; u <= 17; ++u) {\n                ll coeff = arr[u][mask];\n                for (int v = 0; u + v <= 17; ++v)\n                    dp[j][u+v] = (dp[j][u+v] + coeff * dp[j-1][v]) % MOD;\n            }\n        }\n        b[mask] = dp[k][target];\n    }\n    for (int bit = 0; bit < 17; ++bit) {\n        for (int mask = 0; mask < (1 << 17); ++mask) {\n            if ((mask >> bit) & 1)\n                b[mask] = (b[mask] - b[mask ^ (1 << bit)]) % MOD;\n        }\n    }\n    ll ans = (power(k, n*2) - (b[n] % MOD) * fact[n*2] % MOD + MOD) % MOD;\n    cout << ans << \"\\n\";\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = int(data[0])\n    k = int(data[1])\n    MOD = int(data[2])\n    \n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        print(pow(k, n, MOD))\n        return\n    \n    # factorials up to original n\n    fact = [1] * (n + 1)\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        fact[i] = fact[i-1] * i % MOD\n    inv_fact = [1] * (n + 1)\n    inv_fact[n] = pow(fact[n], MOD-2, MOD)\n    for i in range(n-1, -1, -1):\n        inv_fact[i] = inv_fact[i+1] * (i+1) % MOD\n    \n    original_n = n\n    n >>= 1  # halve n\n    \n    MAX_BITS = 17\n    SIZE = 1 << MAX_BITS\n    \n    # arr[pc][mask] for pc = 0..17, mask = 0..SIZE-1\n    arr = [[0] * SIZE for _ in range(MAX_BITS + 1)]\n    for i in range(n + 1):\n        pc = i.bit_count()\n        arr[pc][i] = inv_fact[i * 2]\n    \n    # SOS DP on arr\n    for pc in range(MAX_BITS + 1):\n        for bit in range(MAX_BITS):\n            step = 1 << bit\n            for mask in range(SIZE):\n                if mask & step:\n                    arr[pc][mask] += arr[pc][mask ^ step]\n        for mask in range(SIZE):\n            arr[pc][mask] %= MOD\n    \n    target = n.bit_count()\n    \n    b = [0] * SIZE\n    # dp[j][v] for j=0..k, v=0..17\n    for mask in range(SIZE):\n        dp = [[0] * (MAX_BITS + 1) for _ in range(k + 1)]\n        dp[0][0] = 1\n        for j in range(1, k + 1):\n            for u in range(MAX_BITS + 1):\n                coeff = arr[u][mask]\n                if coeff == 0:\n                    continue\n                # v from 0 to MAX_BITS - u\n                max_v = MAX_BITS - u\n                for v in range(max_v + 1):\n                    dp[j][u + v] = (dp[j][u + v] + coeff * dp[j-1][v]) % MOD\n        b[mask] = dp[k][target] % MOD\n    \n    # Inverse SOS (Mobius transform)\n    for bit in range(MAX_BITS):\n        step = 1 << bit\n        for mask in range(SIZE):\n            if mask & step:\n                b[mask] = (b[mask] - b[mask ^ step]) % MOD\n    \n    ans = (pow(k, original_n, MOD) - (b[n] % MOD) * fact[original_n] % MOD + MOD) % MOD\n    print(ans)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-4.684815212385729e-05, 0.0, 0.0, -0.00021264675888232887, -0.0004354958946350962, 0.0, -0.006747201085090637, -0.005273005459457636, -0.8837355375289917, -0.10020949691534042, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -0.0017084777355194092, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.000912250077817589, 0.0, -0.002838275395333767, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.16022491455078125, -8.344646857949556e-07, 0.0, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.0005631053354591131, -4.541770613286644e-05, 0.0, -0.0004306104383431375, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.025371909141540527, -0.27977830171585